# 🟦 Nmap — CPTS Cheat Sheet

> 🟢 **Enumeration** · 🔵 **Scanning** · 🟡 **Analysis** · 🔴 **Evasion** · 🟣 **NSE** · ⚫ **Output**

---

# 🔵 1. Basic Nmap

| Command                  | Explanation                   |
| ------------------------ | ----------------------------- |
| `nmap <TARGET>`          | 🔵 Basic TCP scan             |
| `sudo nmap <TARGET>`     | 🔵 Run with root privileges   |
| `nmap -v <TARGET>`       | 🟡 Verbose output             |
| `nmap -vv <TARGET>`      | 🟡 Very verbose output        |
| `nmap -n <TARGET>`       | 🟡 Disable DNS resolution     |
| `nmap -Pn <TARGET>`      | 🔵 Skip host discovery        |
| `nmap --reason <TARGET>` | 🟡 Show reason for port state |

---

# 🟢 2. Host Discovery

| Command                        | Explanation                 |
| ------------------------------ | --------------------------- |
| `sudo nmap -sn <TARGET>`       | 🟢 Discover live hosts only |
| `sudo nmap -PE <TARGET>`       | 🟢 ICMP Echo discovery      |
| `sudo nmap -Pn <TARGET>`       | 🟢 Assume target is online  |
| `sudo nmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24` | 🟢 Discover hosts in subnet |
| `sudo nmap -iL hosts.txt`      | 🟢 Scan targets from file   |

### 🧠 Remember

```text
🟢 -sn = Discover hosts
🟢 -Pn = Assume host is up
```

---

# 🔵 3. TCP Port Scanning

| Command                              | Explanation                  |
| ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------- |
| `sudo nmap -sS <TARGET>`             | 🔵 TCP SYN scan              |
| `sudo nmap -sT <TARGET>`             | 🔵 TCP Connect scan          |
| `sudo nmap -p 80 <TARGET>`           | 🔵 Scan port 80              |
| `sudo nmap -p 22,80,443 <TARGET>`    | 🔵 Scan selected ports       |
| `sudo nmap -p 1-1000 <TARGET>`       | 🔵 Scan ports 1–1000         |
| `sudo nmap -p- <TARGET>`             | 🔵 Scan all 65,535 TCP ports |
| `sudo nmap --top-ports 100 <TARGET>` | 🔵 Scan top 100 ports        |

### SYN Scan Logic

```text
🔵 SYN
   │
   ├── SYN/ACK → 🟢 OPEN
   │
   ├── RST     → ⚫ CLOSED
   │
   └── No response → 🔴 FILTERED
```

---

# 🔵 4. UDP Scanning

| Command                               | Explanation                |
| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| `sudo nmap -sU <TARGET>`              | 🔵 UDP scan                |
| `sudo nmap -sU -p53 <TARGET>`         | 🔵 Scan UDP 53             |
| `sudo nmap -sU -p53,161,500 <TARGET>` | 🔵 Scan selected UDP ports |
| `sudo nmap -sU -p- <TARGET>`          | 🔵 Scan all UDP ports      |

### Common UDP Ports

|    Port | Service |
| ------: | ------- |
|    `53` | DNS     |
| `67/68` | DHCP    |
|    `69` | TFTP    |
|   `123` | NTP     |
|   `161` | SNMP    |
|   `500` | ISAKMP  |

> 🟡 UDP scanning is generally much slower than TCP scanning.

