# 🟣 6. NSE — Nmap Scripting Engine

> NSE extends Nmap with scripts for enumeration, discovery, authentication, vulnerability detection, and more.

### Basic NSE

```bash
nmap -sC <TARGET>
```

🟣 Run default NSE scripts.

```bash
nmap --script <SCRIPT> <TARGET>
```

🟣 Run a specific script.

```bash
nmap --script <SCRIPT1>,<SCRIPT2> <TARGET>
```

🟣 Run multiple scripts.

### Useful Categories

| Category    | Purpose                   |
| ----------- | ------------------------- |
| `default`   | 🟢 Standard enumeration   |
| `discovery` | 🟢 Information discovery  |
| `safe`      | 🟢 Generally safe checks  |
| `version`   | 🟢 Version-related checks |
| `auth`      | 🟡 Authentication checks  |
| `brute`     | 🟡 Brute-force scripts    |
| `vuln`      | 🔴 Vulnerability checks   |

Example:

```bash
sudo nmap --script vuln -p<PORTS> <TARGET>
```

> ⚠️ `dos`, `exploit`, `fuzzer`, and `intrusive` scripts may be disruptive.

