# 🔴 13. Firewall / IDS / IPS Evasion

> ⚠️ Use these techniques only against systems you are authorized to test, such as HTB/THM labs or an approved assessment.

## ACK Scan

```bash
sudo nmap -sA -p443 <TARGET>
```

Helps determine:

```text
🔴 FILTERED
      vs
🟢 UNFILTERED
```

> `-sA` does **not** directly determine whether a port is open.

---

## Source Port Manipulation

```bash
sudo nmap -sS -p443 --source-port 53 <TARGET>
```

🔴 Forces source port `53`.

Useful against poorly configured firewall rules that trust traffic from particular source ports.

---

## Packet Fragmentation

```bash
sudo nmap -sS -f <TARGET>
```

🔴 Fragment IP packets.

```bash
sudo nmap -sS --mtu 8 <TARGET>
```

🔴 Specify fragment size.

---

## Decoys

```bash
sudo nmap -sS -D RND:5 <TARGET>
```

🔴 Generate random decoy sources.

Concept:

```text
Your scan
    +
Decoy
    +
Decoy
    +
Decoy
```

---

## Source IP

```bash
sudo nmap -S <SOURCE_IP> <TARGET>
```

🔴 Specify source IP.

---

## Network Interface

```bash
sudo nmap -e tun0 <TARGET>
```

🔵 Specify network interface.

Useful when working through an HTB VPN interface.

