# 🟡 14. Firewall State Interpretation

| State                 | Meaning                              |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| 🟢 `open`             | Service is listening                 |
| ⚫ `closed`            | Host reachable, no service listening |
| 🔴 `filtered`         | Filtering prevents determining state |
| 🟡 `open\|filtered`   | Cannot distinguish                   |
| 🟡 `closed\|filtered` | Cannot distinguish                   |

### Quick Logic

```text
🟢 OPEN
   ↓
Service responds

⚫ CLOSED
   ↓
Host responds but no service

🔴 FILTERED
   ↓
Firewall / filter interferes
```

---

# 🟡 15. `--reason`

```bash
sudo nmap --reason <TARGET>
```

Example:

```text
PORT   STATE     SERVICE  REASON
22/tcp open      ssh      syn-ack
80/tcp open      http     syn-ack
21/tcp closed    ftp      reset
443/tcp filtered https    no-response
```

### Interpretation

| Reason             | Meaning                           |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------- |
| `syn-ack`          | 🟢 SYN/ACK received → open        |
| `reset`            | ⚫ TCP RST received → closed       |
| `no-response`      | 🔴 No response → likely filtering |
| `admin-prohibited` | 🔴 Traffic explicitly prohibited  |

