# 🟡 20. Scan Output Interpretation

## Example — Open

```text
22/tcp open ssh OpenSSH 8.2p1 Ubuntu
```

Think:

```text
🟢 OPEN
   ↓
SSH is listening
   ↓
OpenSSH 8.2p1
   ↓
Enumerate SSH
```

---

## Example — Closed

```text
21/tcp closed ftp
```

Think:

```text
⚫ CLOSED
   ↓
Host is reachable
   ↓
No FTP service listening
```

---

## Example — Filtered

```text
443/tcp filtered https
```

Think:

```text
🔴 FILTERED
   ↓
Firewall / ACL / IDS / IPS?
   ↓
Investigate
```

---

## Example — UDP

```text
53/udp open|filtered domain
```

Think:

```text
🟡 OPEN|FILTERED
       ↓
UDP response insufficient
       ↓
Use -sV / NSE
```

---

## Example — Hidden Service

```text
50000/tcp filtered
```

Think:

```text
🔴 FILTERED
     ↓
Unusual high port
     ↓
Possible firewall filtering
     ↓
Investigate with appropriate technique
     ↓
Re-enumerate
```

